# Status feedback — use StatusModal

When showing **success**, **error**, or **alert/warning** outcome to the user (after an action, submission, or background job start):

- Use `StatusModal` from `src/core/shared/components/ui/status-modal.tsx`
- Do **not** create feature-specific status dialogs (no duplicate modal markup)
- Do **not** use inline alerts alone when the outcome deserves a dedicated modal (e.g. run started, upload failed)

## Variants

| Variant | Use when |
|---------|----------|
| `success` | Action completed or started successfully |
| `error` | Action failed; offer retry when applicable |
| `alert` | Non-blocking warning or attention needed |

## Layout

1. **Surface icon** — colored by variant (`success` green, `error` red, `alert` yellow) via `SurfaceIcon`
2. **Title** + **description**
3. **Optional content** (`children`) — omit when title + description are enough (e.g. agent run started)
4. **Footer actions** — primary + secondary buttons

## Pattern

```tsx
import { StatusModal } from "src/core/shared/components/ui/status-modal";

<StatusModal
  open={open}
  variant="success"
  title={t("title")}
  description={t("description")}
  onClose={handleClose}
  secondaryAction={{ label: t("close"), onClick: handleClose }}
  primaryAction={{ label: t("continue"), onClick: handleContinue }}
>
  {/* optional — only when extra body is needed */}
</StatusModal>
```

Feature modules may wrap `StatusModal` with domain i18n (see `cuts-run-status-modal.tsx`) — the shared component owns surface icon, layout, and footer actions. Agent status modals should **not** pass `children`.

Reference: `confirmation-dialog.tsx` for dialog conventions; `dialog.tsx` primitives.
